The `omitzero` struct tag only checks reflect.Value.IsZero() and ignores a type's own custom IsZero() method, so fields of types that define their own zero-ness logic aren't omitted/included correctly when marshaling. For example:

type customZeroType struct { Value int }
func (c customZeroType) IsZero() bool { return c.Value < 10 }

type doc struct { Custom customZeroType `toml:",omitzero"` }
toml.Marshal(doc{Custom: customZeroType{Value: 5}})

Since Value=5 makes the custom IsZero() return true, the Custom field should be omitted from the output, but it currently isn't (similarly, a pointer-receiver IsZero() method should also be respected). Please make omitzero honor a type's custom IsZero() method when present, similar to how encoding/json handles this.
